From cd6ea3c35f47444b714be5643832a055dba5d773 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: csolomon <charliesolomon@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 09:35:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] offline-model-data: build without the vendor catalogue fetch

Re-authored 2026-09-02: gah-model-data.ts now writes src/providers/data/
in place instead of staging under a mkdtemp directory and swapping it in.
On a managed Windows machine the final rmSync of the staging directory
failed with EPERM ("Permission denied: ...\.model-generation-XXXX"),
which is what antivirus holding a handle on just-scanned files looks like.
The output is deterministic so there is nothing to roll back to; stale
provider files from an earlier hydration are unlinked individually, and
the result is validated the same way. No directory rename or recursive
delete remains in the step.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011it956DeV4unyWw5VyvkDD
